Subject: [PATCH] AccessControl: allow API tokens to call PUT /access/password

The change_password endpoint has allowtoken => 0, which prevents any API
token from changing user passwords. This is overly restrictive for
administrative automation — tokens with the required permissions
(Realm.AllocateUser + User.Modify, or changing a user they own) should be
able to change passwords.

The existing ACL permission checks are sufficient protection:
  - ['userid-param', 'self']   OR
  - Realm.AllocateUser + User.Modify on a group the target user belongs to

Note: PAM realm passwords are still blocked (existing check in the code body)
since PAM passwords are system-level and should not be changed via automation.

--- a/usr/share/perl5/PVE/API2/AccessControl.pm
+++ b/usr/share/perl5/PVE/API2/AccessControl.pm
@@ change_password method registration:
-    protected => 1, # else we can't access shadow files
-    allowtoken => 0, # we don't want tokens to change the regular user password
-    description => "Change user password.",
+    protected => 1, # else we can't access shadow files
+    allowtoken => 1, # tokens with sufficient ACL permissions may change passwords
+    description => "Change user password.",
